{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874987-custom-lair-traits","id":874987,"title":"Custom Lair Traits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-26T16:34:45-07:00","id":874987,"title":"Custom Lair Traits","content":"Post your homebrewed Lair Traits here.<br /> <br /> <b>Isolated (Minor Lair Trait)</b><br /> <br /> Whether a thousand miles from civilization or trapped in an abandoned building with crappy cell reception, it is impossible to contact help. As long as this Lair Trait is in effect, no mundane means of communicating or perceiving what is actually going on inside or outside the area will work. Supernatural means of perception and communication provoke a Clash of Wills roll.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T17:20:40-07:00","id":875025,"title":"","content":"How about a <b>Mutation</b> Major Trait? It could give a number of stationary devices equal to Lair that can transform people according to the mechanics of the &quot;Divine Clay&quot; and &quot;Shifting&quot; Dread Powers of the Idigam. The devices can take many forms: an operating table with mechanical limbs covered in surgical tools, witch cauldrons filled with thick bubbling liquids and half-dissolved animal parts or a bed of maggots that wrap you in a cocoon. I'm not sure of how long these mutations would last outside of the Lair, or if this is better as an Atavism. I personally prefer it as a Lair Trait. It's a horrific reminder that being devoured is not the worst that can happen if you're kidnapped by a monster.<br /> <br /> To make it more versatile, it could also give positive modifications, such as Striking Looks and Hardy, but only if the Beast allows it. This might work better as a &quot;wishing well&quot; sort of Lair Trait, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-26-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:43:49-07:00","id":875570,"title":"","content":"Question: can people actually LIVE in Lairs? Like, welcomed guests, can you treat them like staff if you allow them inside via Primordial Gateway, etc? If possible, that might be something worth developing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:46:46-07:00","id":875572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874987-custom-lair-traits?p=875570#post875570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: can people actually LIVE in Lairs? Like, welcomed guests, can you treat them like staff if you allow them inside via Primordial Gateway, etc? If possible, that might be something worth developing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, so long as you can either have Horror not hunt you or be able to fight it off. Food and water might be an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:00:31-07:00","id":875587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874987-custom-lair-traits?p=875572#post875572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could, so long as you can either have Horror not hunt you or be able to fight it off. Food and water might be an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't it be possible to feed off the terrain? Granted, it's dreamstuff, but given the supernatural nature of said-stuff, you <i>could</i> get away with it, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 04-27-2016, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:02:18-07:00","id":875589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874987-custom-lair-traits?p=875587#post875587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it be possible to feed off the terrain? Granted, it's dreamstuff, but given the supernatural nature of said-stuff, could you get away with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could. It's still difficult to find food on the side of a volcano with ash choking the air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:05:44-07:00","id":875591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874987-custom-lair-traits?p=875589#post875589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could. It's still difficult to find food on the side of a volcano with ash choking the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's like the realms of Arcadia and their &quot;Law of Hospitality&quot;. Either that, or because the Beast welcomes the target, his/her lair subtly changes to accomodate--eg, the guest'll find a rare piece of vegetation by what feels like sheer luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T16:29:51-07:00","id":876107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/874987-custom-lair-traits?p=875570#post875570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: can people actually LIVE in Lairs? Like, welcomed guests, can you treat them like staff if you allow them inside via Primordial Gateway, etc? If possible, that might be something worth developing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always keep a crate of non-perishable foods in your Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T12:49:48-07:00","id":1135879,"title":"","content":"That's cool!<br /> <br /> Necromancing this thread since I thought having a homebrew Lair Trait thread would be nice.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait#post649174\">Wondrous</a> Lair Trait is extremely sweet imo!<br /> <br /> I'd like to make a Time Distortion Lair Trait, where Time flows differently in the Lair, effectively making everything go in fast-forward or in slow-motion. Both have their benefits, so the Beast would have to chose when taking the trait. Any ideas on how to represent that mechanically? +x to speed, but -x to Wit-based dicerolls?<br /> <br /> Also, an Anti-Gravity one, which would heavily affect, among other things, accuracy of ranged weapons and movement.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other possibilities:<br /> <br /> Irradiated - The Lair is heavily irradiated. Major Trait. Extreme Environment 2-4.<br /> <br /> Explosions - Be they artillery shells, fireballs or explosive little common dragons, the Beast's Lair is a source of constant explosions. Major Trait. Deals 2L physical damage every other round, and inflicts the Knockdown tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-27T14:39:18-07:00","id":1560236,"title":"","content":"I had this one in mind<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Magical Background (Major Lair Trait)</b>:Either than the aura of the land or the magical miasma of the air, Supernatural Effects made by those that have Kinship with the Beast gain a +1 on rolls and the caster add the Beast\u2019s Lair trait as a penalty to rolls to resist the effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-28T20:20:29-07:00","id":1560250,"title":"","content":"<b>Squishy (Major Lair Trait):</b> the landscape of this Lair has a rubbery, almost dough-like consistency, that makes it nearly impossible for unwelcomed guests to maintain a stable foothold while traversing it. The walls, floor and ceiling give way beneath their touch, molding themselves around the trespasser's limbs to deny them solid purchase. This trait adds a +2 difficulty to all rolls involving Athletics made by the Beast's enemies, so long as they remain exposed to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Entrancing (Minor Lair Trait):</b> it is said that some creatures, such as the infamous Will-O-Wisp hypnotize people before luring them away to their deaths. This trait mimics those legends by ensnaring the victim's mind and convincing them to deliberately walk right into the Beast's trap. Once per scene, this trait allows the Beast to make a <i>Presence + Manipulation</i> roll against a target's <i>Wits + Resolve.</i> If the target fails the contest, they fall into a trance-like state as they follow the Beast into its Lair, paying no heed to any possible dangers that might be waiting to ambush them upon their arrival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-01T23:33:00-08:00","id":1565077,"title":"","content":"<b>Eldritch (Major Lair Trait):</b> the landscape is nightmarishly <i>wrong</i>. Not just creepy, or eerie, but deeply unsettling. Be it meatmoss walls and living-fleshcraft-interior design, non-corporeal existence, jump-scaring tentacles and tendrils, or something that enhances the cosmic insignificance by making the affected aware of the sheer scale of the universe(s), it takes all of one's willpower not to go mad. This trait denies Willpower use, and a +2 difficulty to all Perception rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Time Distortion (Major Lair Trait):</b> Time flows disturbingly differently: maybe moving feels like watching oneself in slow motion, unable to react any faster but forced to experience everything in excrutiating detail, or things are sped up to the point walking becomes a severe reaction challenge, or time is just wonky in general, the result is always that the normal coordination one relies on to move is off-timing and one needs to enter &quot;manual mode&quot; to navigate this place. Speed is halved, and any physical action requires an Wits+Athletics roll. On a critical failure, the intended action critically fails instead. On a failure, the action automatically fails (you may not roll). If the action was to move, the character stumbles and does not move. On a success, the intended action takes place as normal (if it would require a roll, you may now make the roll). On a critical success, the character's brain adapts to the changed timeflow and may forego the Wits+Athletics check until the trait expires (their speed remains halved).<br /> <br /> <b>Explosions (Major Lair Trait):</b> Be they artillery shells, fireballs or explosive little common dragons, the Beast's Lair is a source of constant explosions. Every round, roll Wits + Dexterity to try and evade incoming eplosions. On a critical success, avoid all damage and gain the Steadfast Condition. On a success, avoid all damage as you get out of the way in time. On a failure, take 2L damage. On a critical failure, deals 2L physical damage every other round, and inflicts the Knockdown tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 11-02-2026, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}